Z||000000||Denise||11-12-2000||11:54 AM||||in my previous post i asked some questions. no answers.. <BR>I know many have used the 5spd iszsu trans with the 2.8 (even with the v8's) i'm wondering what kinds of clutch problems, solutions others have found.  Seems like the TO bearing for the Iszsu trans is not big enough to properly engage the fingers onlarger clutch PP from the 6 cyl set up.  <BR>thanks again!!<BR>Denise<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||11-12-2000||01:08 PM||||Trust me, Denise...these guys NEVER ignore a female needing assistance. It's just that of those of us who have read your post, we probably don't know the answer for sure. I bet if you called or emailed Rodney Dickman or Ed Parks, they could tell you.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||11-12-2000||03:02 PM||||I believe that it was said in a previous post that the clutch for the transmission must be used, regardless of which engine you have. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||pherder||11-12-2000||03:05 PM||||I am running a 97 <B>Isuzu 5 speed</B>, <B>Isuzu throwout bearing</B> and the GM replacement <B>Centerforce dual friction Clutch</B>/Pressure Plate (there is only one number and it is used for the 2.8 and the 2.3 Quad 4) in my 88 Coupe with an HO Quad 4.  No problems using the clutch ... yet.  Not many miles on the combo since the throttle cable is coming apart and hanging the throttle open at about 2K RPM.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||11-12-2000||05:31 PM||||Paul, did you mean 97 or 87 tranny? That's good news that you got your quad 4 Fiero going. I know you were really struggling with it for awhile.<P>Denise, since Cooter and Paul have reminded me, I now remember other people saying the same thing. You need to ask for the clutch and throw-out bearing for the Isuzu 5-speed. Tell the auto parts counter you need parts for a Fiero with a 2.5 four cylinder with a 5-speed.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Denise||11-12-2000||06:06 PM||||Thanks Guys...   I have in my possesson now,  a RAM Heavy duty clutch from the Fiero store, it's for the 5 spd iszsu transmission.  They insist this is the one to use with the v6 also.   <BR>Ed parks told me to use the 6 cyl clutch and the iszsu TO bearing.  I've looked at 3 Iszsu TO bearings, they are all too small for the 6cyl clutch plate fingers..  I'm starting to loose sleep about clutch diameter and torque..  everyone tells me so far "it's OK" but i'm not so sure.. But i'm going to have it put in.<P>By the way.. what is the part # for a new flywheel?  and source?  <BR>thanks allot!!<BR>"I really love you guys!!"   (re: jim carey)<BR>Denise<P>------------------<BR>Denise,Blk 86 Fiero SE, was 4 spd now 5 spd (iszsu) jasper 2.8,BFG TA's, yada yada yada..||||reg||1
